{
 "note": "Milestone 70, 70A: the delivery owner's review of tests/baseline/ms70-declaration-dispositions.json. The draft places each declaration by the monolith section it sits in; the review found that rule wrong for 94 declarations (sections whose banner no longer describes what is under them) and one disposition (_visitedPages, dead). scripts/ms70-declaration-dispositions.mjs applies these overrides and marks a declaration reviewed only while its disposition and delivery still match what is recorded here, so a declaration that appears later starts unreviewed and fails tests/unit/ms70-declaration-dispositions.spec.js.",
 "reviewedBy": "Claude (Milestone 70 delivery owner)",
 "reviewedOn": "2026-09-24",
 "method": "Every section's declarations were read against the plan's delivery scopes (MILESTONE-70-PROPOSAL.md, 'Delivery map'); every delete-as-dead and test-only candidate was searched for by name across src, index.html, fragments, help and tests, markup and window reads included; each duplicate keeps its duplicateOf module as the canonical home.",
 "why": {
  "state-owner": "The case-state root. 70E adopts a store seam while this stays the owner; the declaration goes when the module store becomes the sole owner (70J), not with the section it happens to sit in.",
  "router-state": "Navigation state the router owns (src/core/navigation/router.js reads and writes it); moves with the router in 70K.",
  "persistence": "Save, auto-save, export-dirty tracking, template loading or the continue prompt -- persistence and startup (70I), not the section it sits in.",
  "store-seam": "An accessor modules call to read case state: exactly what 70E's store seam replaces.",
  "shell": "Sidebar, header, picker or tab-coordination UI -- a shell controller (70H). The router banner above it is historical: the router itself moved to src/core/navigation/router.js.",
  "registry": "Filing-type registry data, a blank factory or a normalizer: 70C's scope (normalizeWardData is the .sav-load normalizer).",
  "pure": "A pure calculation or formatter with no DOM or state: 70B.",
  "form-runtime": "Form-field markup, field helpers or collection add/remove actions -- the shared form runtime (70F). They sit in the feature-bridge sections only because they were left behind when each feature was extracted.",
  "bridge": "A feature bridge like the other seven, which move together in 70K; the Simplified one sits in the Guardian wizard's section by accident.",
  "dead-visited": "Dead on both sides: a `let` is never a window property, so the three module references (router.js add, ward-lifecycle.js clear x2) read window._visitedPages as undefined and never run, and the monolith never reads it. Delete it and those three references together in 70E."
 },
